<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:31Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany news: Deportations on the decline</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d86dd6d9ba0c50d1b40027f807eefafba04dbd8f6d7381a28c52a57dc45777d</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T09:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-deportations-on-the-decline/live-79860126--231ad2fcde65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-deportations-on-the-decline/live-79860126?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite a decrease in overall deportations, more people were sent back to Turkey. Meanwhile, Volkswagen is facing a fresh 'Dieselgate' trial. And Germany's leading DAX stock index hit a new high. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bavarian politician Hubert Aiwanger found dead in Berlin hotel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce3c919809177a25b435cb4f9c0131502c47858ecb9a36f513904038d9fd5d38</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bavarian-politician-hubert-aiwanger-found-dead-in-berlin-hotel/a-79859115--a5e0e6ba38b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bavarian-politician-hubert-aiwanger-found-dead-in-berlin-hotel/a-79859115?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Aiwanger was Bavaria's Economy Minister and the chairman of the right-wing populist Free Voters party. The circumstances surrounding his death are still unclear.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Commerce chief hopes for more stable US trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bef1b7b034497f694d3bd631a044988dc391cdb6d352df84012e10bc418c8ef6</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-commerce-chief-hopes-for-more-stable-us-trade/live-79854127--6b9f63120529.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-commerce-chief-hopes-for-more-stable-us-trade/live-79854127?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German business is pinning its hopes on greater stability in US trade relations after a midterm blow for Donald Trump. Meanwhile, Germany's automakers appear to be feeling less gloomy than in recent years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>BMW reports lower Q3 earnings as China woes mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30e1cefcf723c926c53250cc07dd16ad5393544f5200606cf3f8cc0a9a584e09</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bmw-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847--9f74c40c2952.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bmw-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">BMW reports a drop in profits in the July to September quarter amid fierce competition from China.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Pioneering Jewish academy opens in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65e9f30b18582d4e6b35821b88bf125fdecf75122ece581cb3716dff10073b6b</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pioneering-jewish-academy-opens-in-germany/a-79863293--10bb65c14f4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pioneering-jewish-academy-opens-in-germany/a-79863293?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Jewish academy has opened its doors in Frankfurt. The Central Council of Jews in Germany, the country’s leading Jewish umbrella group, set up the project to combat hate and promote dialogue and learning nationally.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The 2011 discovery of neo-Nazi killers aired biases in German policing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:185f98344238dfde3289af4e6037dfe2891eb4db881ac7bdca1be3bf791d2040</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-2011-discovery-of-neo-nazi-killers-aired-biases-in-german-policing/a-79857781--949d4ea66003.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-2011-discovery-of-neo-nazi-killers-aired-biases-in-german-policing/a-79857781?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Many questions still surround the National Socialist Underground whose existence was revealed by neo-Nazi terrorist Beate Zschäpe on November 4, 2011. How has German society reacted to NSU crimes? Has justice been done?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's celebrated children's author Janosch has died</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57263e6c49cb4edfe302c1ef01f5ea38d1dd764b6cc6808449dbd3d66eb90812</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600--a3fdc8a2501b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bear, Tiger and Tiger-Duck: The author and illustrator Janosch achieved world fame with his heartwarming children's figures. He died at the age of 95.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine war: Merz doubts Russia is serious about a truce</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59503ed857a4650adab6d932d3af583fdab0b5935079211139aa2cd4ab0cc789</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-war-merz-doubts-russia-is-serious-about-a-truce/a-79836026--11d120b4fdbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-war-merz-doubts-russia-is-serious-about-a-truce/a-79836026?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz met with Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Berlin. Both leaders said the EU needs to be included in peace talks with Russia. Merz also expressed doubts that Russia is serious about seeking a truce.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How Berlin's Arab queers are building their community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f272f3c6adab7286d9660fd46ec10f66a685510521e990bd4ef1e93613d0451a</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143--c676c7f349f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the co-founder of the ADIRA Drag Festival, Lebanese performance artist, drag performer, DJ and cultural organizer Hassandra has become an essential part of Berlin's queer artistic landscape.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>The dachshund, a humorous icon with political symbolism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcad094f4a9f7f57f486e175adf4a7fddc27e16b2628019f32c6322923422652</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T07:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191--0ec0144d606e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Picasso to Andy Warhol, a surprising number of artists have portrayed the German breed. But the dachshund has also at times been co-opted as a political symbol.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Wagner brothers begin new NBA chapter on different paths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1c4a17104858ee9be801111eec1c5da027abd9daf4fc2dfb72f9d6edb16e75a</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668--ff5544415c4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After five years, brothers Franz and Moritz Wagner are no longer playing together for the Orlando Magic. In the new NBA season, their separation will likely mean the new "German" team is the Charlotte Hornets.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
